      ],
      "spacing": {
        "top": "large",
        "bottom": "large"
      },
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "h4",
          "html": "A Slate should be filmed separately from the audition sides.",
          "align": "center"
        },
        {
          "type": "blockquote",
          "html": "Repeating slate over and over before a scene reading pulls an Actor out of Scene preparation and Character."
        },
        {
          "type": "h4",
          "html": "In a Self Tape the Slate is the one opportunity an Actor has to show their charisma and vibe with the Casting Director."
        },
        {
          "type": "blockquote",
          "html": "In the Casting Room, conversation and personal interaction is a Huge component in a potential callback"
        },
        {
          "type": "h4",
          "html": "You must use the Slate as your one opportunity to have them see who you are and why they should want to get to know you"
        },
        {
          "type": "blockquote",
          "html": "Don’t be afraid to stand out. Adding a few seconds of personality never hurt anybody."
        }
      ]
    },
